      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Why does my WhatsApp bot fail 40 % of the time during M-Pesa webhook storms?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Safaricom’s STK callback API returns 503 with Retry-After: 30 during load spikes, and naive retries with axios-retry default settings hammer the retry budget. Each retry sends the same 1.2 k token payload, so at 800 req/min you burn 960 k tokens in one minute—roughly 1 152 KES at 2026 token prices. The fix is to use a token-aware queue with backpressure: when the queue depth exceeds 100, switch to a 30-second fixed delay instead of exponential and cap max retries at 3. In Python 3.12 with httpx and tenacity: python from tenacity import retry, stopafterattempt, waitfixed @retry(stop=stopafterattempt(3), wait=waitfixed(30)) async def confirmpayment(payload: dict) -> bool: async with httpx.AsyncClient(timeout=5.0) as client: r = await client.post(mpesawebhook, json=payload) r.raiseforstatus() return True"
      }
