      "name": "When does it make sense to fine-tune an embedding model instead of using a prompt template?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Fine-tuning bge-small-en-v1.5 on Swahili cut retrieval error 12 % but raised English error 8 %, a net loss for bilingual users. The break-even point is 150k in-domain tokens where the accuracy gain outweighs the multilingual regression. If your corpus is <50k tokens, stick to prompt templates; the gain isn’t worth the localisation debt."
      }
